===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Separated from [[reality]] and [[practical]] matters; overly academic.
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1968|journal=New Library World|volume=69-70|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=FR3yAAAAMAAJ&q=%22a+very+ivory+tower%22&dq=%22a+very+ivory+tower%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ZFLNVMXZDISLgwTj34KgDg&ved=0CGEQ6AEwDg|page=8
|passage=The majority of librarians appear to have shown a very '''ivory tower''' approach to the application of all types of management technique to librarianship.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|title=Hearings relating to Madison Guaranty S&L and the Whitewater Development Corporation, Washington, DC phase|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=VauFAAAAIAAJ&q=%22a+very+ivory+tower%22&dq=%22a+very+ivory+tower%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ZFLNVMXZDISLgwTj34KgDg&ved=0CDYQ6AEwBQ|page=504
|passage=I must say that, with all due respect, I think that's a very '''ivory tower''' approach.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=Joan Gorham|title=Annual Editions: Mass Media 07/08|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=-KHhAAAAMAAJ&q=%22a+very+ivory+tower%22&dq=%22a+very+ivory+tower%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=ZFLNVMXZDISLgwTj34KgDg&ved=0CEAQ6AEwBw|page=158
|passage=Bob Woodruff, an anchor and correspondent for ABC News who arrived in New Orleans the Wednesday after the storm hit, calls the detached-observer ideal "a very '''ivory tower''' notion that's not practiced in the field."}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Geoffrey Kabaservice|title=The Guardians|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=wf-WC2xjO4sC&lpg=PA154&dq=%22the%20most%20ivory%20tower%22&pg=PA154#v=onepage&q=%22the%20most%20ivory%20tower%22&f=false|page=154
|passage=Griswold was perhaps the most '''ivory tower''' president of Yale in the twentieth century, and in many ways the university turned toward conservatism in the decade after his inauguration, in 1950.}}

